     {
      "text": "39-year-old male presenting with headache with dizziness for 2 days. Character: throbbing at the back of the head; radiation: to the neck; aggravated by morning time; relieved by rest. Severity 4/10. Associated: blurred vision, palpitations. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 2 years; Hypertension for 5 years. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Amlodipine 5 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: no similar illness. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
